   "title": "Note: a song of your own",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## A song of your own\n\nEach **Lip Service Singer** is one voice and the part it sings. They are chained left to right, the way they are seated. **Choir From Singers** puts them in a room, and **Lip Service Choir** sings them together.\n\n**A part is text:**\n\n- `%bpm 104` sets the tempo and `%rest 1` is a beat of silence.\n- Then a word a line, with a note for each syllable: `lights 66:1` is the word, the note and its beats. Notes are MIDI numbers or names like `F#4`.\n- `+` joins notes on one syllable: `ooh 74:1.5+73:1.5`.\n\nEvery part is written where a woman sings it. A man's voice sings his an octave lower.\n\n**To change it:** edit the words and notes, pick other voices, add a singer by chaining one more. If a word has more syllables than notes, the run stops and says which word and how many.\n\nIt runs on the CPU. No models to download beyond what Lip Service brings."
   ]
  }
